Description:
BlackStill Consulting Services Limited is an independent company providing services in the following areas:

- IT Governance (ISO/IEC 38500);
- Assessment Services (ISO/IEC 20000 and ISO/IEC 27001);
- Information Security Consulting (ISO/IEC 27001);
- IT Service Management Consulting (ITIL and ISO/IEC 20000).

We provide services to a number of clients in the financial, manufacturing, technology and service sectors.
Our objective is to provide a confidential and independent quality service to our clients.

iFeed is a source-backed healthcare intelligence practice for regulated life-sciences and health-tech work.

It turns regulatory signals, quality-system patterns, AI-governance questions, clinical-research evidence and market movement into structured intelligence teams can actually use: source links, obligations, gaps, risks, decision notes and next-action maps.

The current focus is clinical research, bioanalytical and bioequivalence evidence, GxP validation, MedTech quality, AI governance and responsible AI adoption in regulated workflows.

iFeed is built from an operator-grounded quality perspective. The work values audit-readiness, traceability, documentation discipline, source-linked research, human review and practical implementation over generic commentary.

Current workstreams include:

- BE/BMV evidence acceptance across India, EU, US and Brazil;
- AI governance and evidence readiness for regulated life sciences;
- CSV, Part 11, Annex 11 and GAMP 5 validation intelligence;
- quality-system and regulatory-intelligence briefs;
- checklist evaluations, evidence-gap reviews and readiness sprints.

iFeed provides analytical research, intelligence and advisory support. It does not provide legal advice, regulatory representation, notified-body services, conformity assessment, certification, clinical validation or guaranteed compliance outcomes.

Founder: Sunita Nawale, Quality & Trust Systems Architect.
